+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) is that standard, and the upcoming JSON Patch (RFC 6902) work and other features will build on it, so it must exist first and be correct.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`: returns the value a JSON Pointer string refers to in a JSON document.
+- It throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901 §3) or does not resolve to a value of the document (§4).
+- Also export a `JsonPointerError` class (extends `Error`) thrown in both cases, so callers can tell pointer failures apart from other errors.
+- Governing standard: RFC 6901 §3 (syntax), §4 (evaluation). No breaking changes: the library has no existing source or API.
+- Out of scope: the URI fragment representation (§6), creating/updating values through a pointer (JSON Patch), and parsing JSON text (the document is an already-parsed value).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: Parsing and evaluating RFC 6901 JSON Pointer strings against JSON documents.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code in `src/` (and tests runnable by `npm test`); no runtime dependencies added; `package.json` may only change as needed to run TypeScript tests.
+- New public API surface: `resolvePointer`, `JsonPointerError`.
